# No git commit / push

Agents must **never** create commits or push to remotes in this repo.

- Do **not** run `git commit`, `git push`, or equivalents (including amend, hooks bypass, force push).
- Do **not** stage-and-commit workflows even if the user says “commit this” or “ship it”.
- Prepare diffs, messages, and release steps for the user; they commit/push themselves.
- Read-only git (`status`, `diff`, `log`, `show`) and local non-publishing commands are fine.

A project `beforeShellExecution` hook also denies `git commit` / `git push` as a hard stop.
